\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The sun is sinking fast,
\par The daylight dies;
\par Let love awake, and pay
\par Her evening sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As Christ upon the Cross
\par His head inclined
\par And to His Father's hands
\par His parting soul resigned:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So now herself my soul
\par Would wholly give
\par Into His sacred charge
\par In whom all spirits live:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. So now beneath His eye
\par Would calmly rest,
\par Without a wish or thought
\par Abiding in the breast-
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Save that His will be done,
\par Whate'er betide;
\par Dead to herself, and dead
\par In Him to all beside.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thus would I live; yet now
\par Not I, but He,
\par In all His power and love,
\par Henceforth alive in me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. One sacred Trinity,
\par One Lord Divine,
\par Thine may I ever be,
\par And Thou for ever mine.
\par                   Amen. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

